course: dictionary
lesson: 10421
title: Same word, different meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. «Triton» is one of these words. Context, the words and sentences around it, shows you which meaning is right. «Neptune's largest moon Triton orbits backwards» tells you Triton is a moon, because moon and Neptune are close by.
explain: Look at the capital letter too. A capital T often names a particular thing, such as a god or a moon. A small t, as in «a triton», usually means a kind of creature. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
explain: Orbits is another clue. It means goes round something. So Triton goes round Neptune, and the word backwards tells you it goes round in the opposite direction to most moons.
fact: Triton is the largest moon of the planet Neptune. It is icy and very cold.
fact: In myths from ancient Greece, Triton is a sea god, half man and half fish, who blows a conch shell like a trumpet.
fact: A triton is also a large sea snail with a long, pointed shell, called a triton shell.
fact: «Neptune's largest moon Triton orbits backwards» and probably was captured from the Kuiper belt, a ring of icy little worlds beyond Neptune.
fact: Context tells you which meaning of a word is right, so always read the words around it.
exercise: «Neptune's largest moon Triton orbits backwards.» What is Triton? | A large sea snail | A kind of newt | A sea god who blows a shell | *A moon of Neptune
exercise: In Greek myths, Triton is a sea god. What is he half? | Half horse and half eagle | Half tree and half fox | Half bird and half lion | *Half man and half fish
exercise: Find and copy the word in «Neptune's largest moon Triton orbits backwards» that means goes round. | Backwards | Neptune | Largest | *Orbits
test: What does Triton the moon do in a strange way? | It is made of fire | *It orbits Neptune backwards | It is the biggest planet in the sky | It lives under the sea
test: In «the triton shell was long and pointed», what is a triton? | A moon of Neptune | A planet | A sea king in a cartoon | *A large sea snail
exam: In «Triton, moon of Neptune», which clues tell you Triton is a moon? | Its capital T and its long name | The word Triton alone | *The words moon and Neptune | The word of
